WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.939 --> 00:00:01.990
I wanna thank President Trump

2
00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:04.460
for giving me an excuse to visit Greenland.

3
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.450
I went from knowing nothing about a country

4
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:09.600
to falling in love with it in three days.

5
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.500
A special thanks to the people of Greenland

6
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.370
for their generous hospitality

7
00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:16.633
and their even more generous portions of dried fish.

8
00:00:17.546 --> 00:00:20.713
(audience applauding)

9
00:00:22.975 --> 00:00:23.808
Well, this is exciting.

10
00:00:23.808 --> 00:00:24.760
Just touched down in Greenland

11
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.773
and big crowd turned out to greet me.

12
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.613
Settle down, everybody, settle down!

13
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.500
Little known fact about Greenland,

14
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.840
snowmobiles come from all over the world

15
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.540
to this area to mate.
(engines groaning)

16
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.690
It's a six-week rutting season,

17
00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:43.960
they've been going at it.

18
00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.870
They're resting right now.

19
00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:49.310
I wanna give 'em their privacy, so, let's go this way.

20
00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:51.977
(silly singing)

21
00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:56.803
What's happening under the table?

22
00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.560
Young man, what are you doing under the table?

23
00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:00.774
What's his name?

24
00:01:00.774 --> 00:01:01.607
Ian.

25
00:01:01.607 --> 00:01:02.440
Oh, Ian?

26
00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:03.273
Like on Grukka?

27
00:01:03.273 --> 00:01:04.106
Ian, Ian.

28
00:01:04.106 --> 00:01:04.939
Okay, I'm just gonna call him Grukka,

29
00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:07.171
'cause it's just all a mishmash to me.

30
00:01:07.171 --> 00:01:10.180
Grukka, Grukka, what are you doing under the table?

31
00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.690
I want you to come up here and tell us

32
00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.395
what you think about the American foreign policy.

33
00:01:14.395 --> 00:01:15.260
(laughing)

34
00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.547
Grukka, where are you?

35
00:01:16.547 --> 00:01:17.870
Grukka!

36
00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:19.873
Can my wife cook?

37
00:01:19.873 --> 00:01:21.080
What do you care?

38
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.180
You eat raw reindeer liver,

39
00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.262
what do you care if someone cooks?

40
00:01:25.262 --> 00:01:26.350
You know what I mean?

41
00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.240
Yeah, you had an antler for breakfast

42
00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.660
and you're asking if my wife cooks?

43
00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:32.493
What did you have, like?

44
00:01:32.493 --> 00:01:35.940
You had a carp eyeball as a snack an hour ago.

45
00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.510
I saw you eat a rock on the way in.

46
00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:40.220
And you said that you like McDonald's?

47
00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:41.710
Yeah.

48
00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.120
I'm gonna give you this Happy Meal.

49
00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.170
This Happy Meal's for you.
Thank you.

50
00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.730
The only thing I will say,

51
00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:50.580
is we bought it three days ago,

52
00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:53.503
and it's been sitting in a plane, okay?

53
00:01:53.503 --> 00:01:55.280
It got a little hot on the plane

54
00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.020
and this has been smelling weird.

55
00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:59.530
But still, that's my gift to you.

56
00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:00.790
Thank you very much.

57
00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:03.550
You got a Make America Greenland Also hat.

58
00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:06.430
And you got a three-day-old rotting Happy meal.

59
00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:07.780
This is the American dream.

60
00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.880
You have a guitar over there, what's that all about?

61
00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:14.080
Sometimes you need to just relax

62
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:17.510
and play guitar, take a break.

63
00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:18.940
Yeah.
Yeah.

64
00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:20.559
I imagine it gets pretty hectic around here.

65
00:02:20.559 --> 00:02:23.400
It does.

66
00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.754
Anything to sort of take the edge off.

67
00:02:25.754 --> 00:02:27.750
You know, we've been sitting here for a while

68
00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.460
and your phone has not rung once.

69
00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.400
Yeah, I know.

70
00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.130
There's cobwebs all over it.

71
00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:35.080
But when the United Nations declared

72
00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.543
that you should decolonize all your countries,

73
00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:41.100
Denmark figured out a different way to do it.

74
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.430
Basically, we were part of Denmark,

75
00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:45.180
but we were not park of Denmark

76
00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.770
because we were used to be a colony.

77
00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.720
In other words, what you're saying is

78
00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.763
there's something rotten in the state of Denmark.

79
00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.450
But I gotta hit that again

80
00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.350
'cause what you're saying is

81
00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:03.180
there's something rotten in the state of Denmark.

82
00:03:08.691 --> 00:03:09.590
Hey!

83
00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:13.570
No more running to 7-Eleven for bags of ice, America!

84
00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:15.087
We got all we need!

85
00:03:15.087 --> 00:03:18.099
(laughing)

86
00:03:18.099 --> 00:03:20.380
(coughs)

87
00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:21.600
I mean, this is nice,

88
00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.563
but incredible waste of advertising space.

89
00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.967
We'll take care of that.

90
00:03:27.967 --> 00:03:31.140
(billboard humming)

91
00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.100
And I'm bringing you

92
00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.310
the latest weather report for Greenland.

93
00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:39.580
I will give the report in the Greenlandic language.

94
00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:42.106
Let's face it, how hard could it be?

95
00:03:42.106 --> 00:03:44.356
(laughing)

